5. Changed Functions
========================================

- Standard:
  . stream_select() no longer fails once a watched descriptor exceeds
    FD_SETSIZE. The descriptor set now grows on demand on both POSIX (bitset)
    and Windows (winsock fd_set), so code watching many streams works without
    rebuilding PHP with --enable-fd-setsize. On Windows, selecting on more than
    64 pipe or file handles no longer crashes; it fails with a warning, as that
    path remains bounded by WaitForMultipleObjects().

========================================
6. New Functions
========================================

- Intl:
  . Added Transliterator::toRules() and transliterator_to_rules() to export
    rules that can be used to recreate a transliterator. The optional
    $escapeUnprintable argument escapes unprintable characters when true.

========================================
7. New Classes and Interfaces
========================================

- Intl:
  . IntlRelativeDateTimeFormatter
  . enum IntlRelativeDateTimeFormatterStyle
  . enum IntlRelativeDateTimeFormatterCapitalization
  . enum IntlRelativeDateTimeFormatterUnit
    RFC: https://wiki.php.net/rfc/reldateformatter
  . Added IntlNumberFormatter class to format a number with a given locale
    and ICU number skeleton, which also covers measurement units, e.g.
    "measure-unit/speed-kilometer-per-hour unit-width-full-name".
    IntlNumberFormatter::format() accepts an int, a float or a decimal
    string without exponent, the latter being formatted with arbitrary
    precision.
    IntlNumberFormatter::createFromSkeleton() rejects a scale/ option in
    exponent notation, e.g. "scale/1e3".
    It is supported from icu 63.

